          "path": "_m/w/x/4/g/hall-of-supreme-harmony-wp/beijing-2006-2-17.jpg",
          "filename": "Beijing 2006 2-17.jpg",
          "caption": "Painted Decoration. Zhongzuo Gate, Forbidden City, Beijing\nThe decoration seen here is typical of the painting on the eaves and brackets of the\nForbidden City. Underneath the yellow tile roof (this color of roof tile is an imperial perogative),\nbrocade-like patterns of blue, gold, red, white, and green form a bright contrast against\nthe uniform red of the building walls and columns. The paint looks especially fresh due\nto its recent (2006) restoration.\nZhongzuo Gate is located just east of the Hall of Supreme Harmony.",
          "alt": "Painted Decoration. Zhongzuo Gate, Forbidden City, Beijing\nThe decoration seen here is typical of the painting on the eaves and brackets of the\nForbidden City. Underneath the yellow tile roof (this color of roof tile is an imperial perogative),\nbrocade-like patterns of blue, gold, red, white, and green form a bright contrast against\nthe uniform red of the building walls and columns. The paint looks especially fresh due\nto its recent (2006) restoration.\nZhongzuo Gate is located just east of the Hall of Supreme Harmony.",
